WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:09.560
2nd century AD · Llandough hill, above the
Ely Spoken in Welsh, the living descendant
of the Brittonic they spoke

2
00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:19.660
In the 2nd century AD a Roman villa is
built on this hill (MR-0097, PX-02)

3
00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:24.834
[in Welsh] Look at it. A house of stone,
up here on top of the hill.

4
00:00:25.459 --> 00:00:29.512
[in Welsh] Stone lasts. Timber rots and
thatch burns.

5
00:00:29.552 --> 00:00:32.447
This will stand long after we're gone.

6
00:00:38.084 --> 00:00:42.904
[in Welsh] Then let them build it right.
The children will grow up under that roof.

7
00:00:43.543 --> 00:00:47.161
[in Welsh] From the river down there,
they'll see it standing on the hill.

8
00:00:48.343 --> 00:00:57.203
The villa site lies south of where
Llandough's church stands today It is a
separate site from Great House Farm
(PX-02, CH-0174)

